{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts","id":1499531,"title":"Do you ALWAYS \"charge\" XP for Gifts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-13T09:52:49-08:00","id":1499531,"title":"Do you ALWAYS \"charge\" XP for Gifts?","content":"I'm just curious about how you folks work things in your Werewolf games. Do you always make the PC pay the xp for gifts they've learned, or do you let the time/role-play involved cover it from time to time?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27674-johnnyarkham","name":"JohnnyArkham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T13:04:17-08:00","id":1499565,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> From a ton of personal experience, &quot;time/role-play&quot; replacing XP is a slippery slope of bad results. Time and RP is the IC events. Spending XP is the OOC mechanics that govern the events' outcome.<br /> <br /> While rarely necessary for WtA, I find using the XP debt rules from Exalted to cover virtually any instance where this might matter in the WoD and CofD games:<br /> <br /> If the player doesn't have a positive bank of XP to afford something that makes narrative sense for them to learn at that moment, they can have a negative XP value. All future XP rewards must spend at least half of the XP rewarded into paying off the XP debt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T13:04:45-08:00","id":1499566,"title":"","content":"Good question.<br /> From a thematic point of view I find it weird that Gifts always cost XP, thus taking away from your attribute/ability growth you might foster during whatever task you do (sure, the spirit could ask for a little prayer each night for a month, but it might give you some grand heroic journey with plenty of learning experiences)<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I have actually done 1-on-1 games where gifts were gained primarily through gameplay: in one on one games, you can afford to go on your own sidequests.<br /> 1-You become crazily &quot;overpowered&quot; very quickly if you're inclined to it. At least in comparison to the stat blocks of given NPCs.<br /> 2- Quests range from fun to absolute BS. Spirits are weird and some STs struggle to make them work at times. The more you do it, the more the cracks start to show.<br /> <br /> <br /> Related:<br /> Should infernalists pay for their investments or should they do quests for them? If infernalists are losing xp because they're giving pieces of themselves to demons or something, are Garou doing the same with gifts and spirits?<br /> Should vampires pay for Disciplines/atributes or should this be a result of how they diet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 12-13-2022, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T14:49:57-08:00","id":1499576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499566#post1499566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question.<br /> From a thematic point of view I find it weird that Gifts always cost XP, thus taking away from your attribute/ability growth you might foster during whatever task you do (sure, the spirit could ask for a little prayer each night for a month, but it might give you some grand heroic journey with plenty of learning experiences)<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I have actually done 1-on-1 games where gifts were gained primarily through gameplay: in one on one games, you can afford to go on your own sidequests.<br /> 1-You become crazily &quot;overpowered&quot; very quickly if you're inclined to it. At least in comparison to the stat blocks of given NPCs.<br /> 2- Quests range from fun to absolute BS. Spirits are weird and some STs struggle to make them work at times. The more you do it, the more the cracks start to show.<br /> <br /> <br /> Related:<br /> Should infernalists pay for their investments or should they do quests for them? If infernalists are losing xp because they're giving pieces of themselves to demons or something, are Garou doing the same with gifts and spirits?<br /> Should vampires pay for Disciplines/atributes or should this be a result of how they diet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernalists aren't the best of comparisons, because some of the infernalism systems <b>do</b> allow them to do terrible things that further their patron's agenda in exchange for demonic investments (Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition did, I believe; maybe others.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T20:38:22-08:00","id":1499601,"title":"","content":"Yes, on occasion. Usually players spend exp to get Gifts or other stuff, but sometimes I'll give characters freebies during a campaign if the player does something within the context of the story that could earn her something. So if the character impresses a spirit, that spirit might &quot;gift&quot; the character with a Gift. In that case the player gets to add it to the character sheet for free without having to spend exp.<br /> <br /> I tend to keep track of these freebies and try to give out freebies to other characters (maybe a bonus Attribute or Ability, or a bonus background or Merit or something like that) to try and keep things even between the players. This is useful if there's a Gift, or Background or something that I want the players to use in an upcoming session, but they might not choose to spend exp to get it on their own, and I'd feel bad forcing something on them and then demanding that they pay exp for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T21:35:27-08:00","id":1499607,"title":"","content":"I generally expect PCs to pay XP for everything. But like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> I do reward players on occasion for great contributions to the game (generally roleplay but other times for other services or enjoyment to the gaming group). In the Storyteller system, I generally keep that limited to expendable attributes that normally go up and down - Willpower, Humanity, temporary Rage, temporary Gnosis, Backgrounds, etc. But it could include Gifts, especially if those Gifts are out of the ordinary and not something normally available or if I want them to have it for any reason. Like AnubisXy, I try to keep it spread between all the players so people don't resent what they might see as favoritism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T21:36:05-08:00","id":1499608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499576#post1499576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Infernalists aren't the best of comparisons, because some of the infernalism systems <b>do</b> allow them to do terrible things that further their patron's agenda in exchange for demonic investments (Book of the Wyrm 2nd edition did, I believe; maybe others.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Some systems DO allow for it, but aren't Garou essentially doing the same? They're doing tasks to further the spirit's agenda in exchange for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T01:40:35-08:00","id":1499624,"title":"","content":"I also use debt XP if necessary for the story to make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T02:25:09-08:00","id":1499626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499608#post1499608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Some systems DO allow for it, but aren't Garou essentially doing the same? They're doing tasks to further the spirit's agenda in exchange for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not aimed specifically at you MWiS:<br /> <br /> But this is exactly why I don't waive XP costs. Once you start compromising the arbitrary meta nature of XP - as it only exists to mediate character advancement via a mechanic - you undermine the whole concept.<br /> <br /> &quot;If you can get X via IC actions without spending XP, why can't you get Y via IC actions without spending XP?&quot; very quickly leads into the fact that by that logic <b>nothing</b> should cost XP. There's no difference between Infernalists paying evil beings for stuff that normal XP could buy, and rich PCs paying a personal tutor to train them in stuff instead of having to spend XP on it.<br /> <br /> The big draw of things like infernalism or diablerie or whatever, should be getting stuff you can't get otherwise, because that's real temptation.<br /> <br /> If diablerie didn't lower a vampire's Generation, nobody would do it outside of fanatics on certain Paths. It doesn't make sense IC to risk the wrath of your fellow vampires, potential possession by the spirit of the vampire you just ate, and the loss of Humanity (or Path if it's not one that supports diablerie), for some quick XP. You're a vampire. You have the potential to live for centuries. The risks just don't make sense. Even for the players they're trading something worth XP (Humanity) for potential more or less XP worth of other stuff. It wouldn't really be something player's bother with unless they want their Humanity in the dumpster anyway.<br /> <br /> The Generation aspect is the big draw. The only way to do it is diablerie. That's why even the Camarilla will sanction diablerie to entice vampires to hunt down the most dangerous criminals in vampire society without the normal punishments for chowing down on vampire-soul. It would be worth it to a lot of vampires even if you didn't get any free other stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T04:04:38-08:00","id":1499634,"title":"","content":"I do EXP debt for Seekings, and I'd definitely do them for Gifts if it ever came up. That said I've always run it as &quot;you can't spend EXP until your EXP reaches a positive value again&quot;.<br /> <br /> So say you have 1 EXP and through an unpredictable turn of events wind up learning something expensive but story-appropriate; say a level 2 out-of-list gift which made makes perfect sense in the moment. You're down to -9 EXP, and once you earn 9 EXP you're back into the black and can spend EXP normally.<br /> <br /> I've found it's great to be able to do Seekings whenever they make sense, and not just when the EXP and narrative line up together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T04:11:22-08:00","id":1499636,"title":"","content":"I'm on team 'if you don't pay the XP, it doesn't go on the sheet'. I'm also not a big fan of XP debts, but this is the one place where I'll let it slide (although all XP must go towards the debt until it's paid off).<br /> <br /> XP doesn't actually measure anything, it's a mechanic the players use to control the rate of power growth. WoD is somewhat problematic due to it's flat character advancements, but I'm one of the people who houserule most of that out.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I also think that players should be able to go stupid stuff without risking character power. If they'd lose a trait (except morality traits) for any reason they get the XP refunded, although abuse causes traits to stop being lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T17:02:54-08:00","id":1499699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499608#post1499608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Some systems DO allow for it, but aren't Garou essentially doing the same? They're doing tasks to further the spirit's agenda in exchange for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not usually like that, no. Getting an individual meta-currency for improvement tends to imply that the individual is taking strides toward self-improvement, whereas getting a benny for a deed tends to be a bit more... external.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T22:35:53-08:00","id":1499720,"title":"","content":"Backgrounds and rituals don't require XP? Obtaining a shotgun would be a significant boost to your character's capabilities but few would ask XP for it. <br /> <br /> They're called Gifts, right? Do you pay for the gifts other people give you? <br /> <br /> Just playing devil's advocate here. Being someone who's actually done -gifts are earned with RP- i can definetly see why it's not the standard rules. But then again I think a carefully curated -The storyteller tracks what abilities you're using and gives them XP and automatic level-ups- system could be very good (With the player having more freedom to assign xp in downtime). One of the reasons I fell in love with <i>The Elder Scrolls</i> series was that with Morrowind and Oblivion you'd gain skills by using them and powers by buying/finding them, and you could loot everything that wasn't nailed down in Morrowind. It had some problems (Attribute distribution sucked shit) and Skyrim was nothing if not disappointing largely for abandoning what made things great (Perks are more important than skill levels in making you stronger for one)... but I digress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T01:02:17-08:00","id":1499727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499720#post1499720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backgrounds and rituals don't require XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I do prefer the games where these do cost XP, so the people that write the rules did eventually come around to this being a bad idea too.<br /> <br /> Of course, the standard counter points are that Backgrounds can be removed from your sheet because the ST feels like it's justified (which is also why players tend to go hard for Backgrounds that shouldn't be Backgrounds like Generation and Pure Breed, since they not like normal Backgrounds that naturally go up and down as events occur), and learning rites has an insane starting point/XP tax on it already. I've had player beg to have the option of paying XP for rites, because they didn't want to have to buy Intelligence 4 just to have an average chance of learning simple rites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obtaining a shotgun would be a significant boost to your character's capabilities but few would ask XP for it. </div> </div> </div>A shotgun isn't a character Trait in the WoD games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're called Gifts, right? Do you pay for the gifts other people give you? </div> </div> </div>And the names are really bad descriptors of what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just playing devil's advocate here. </div> </div> </div>As tends to get said plenty: the world is in a state where the Devil does not need even more advocates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then again I think a carefully curated -The storyteller tracks what abilities you're using and gives them XP and automatic level-ups- system could be very good (With the player having more freedom to assign xp in downtime). </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of RPGs out there that do some sort of &quot;use traits to raise them,&quot; schemes.<br /> <br /> The big downside is that unlike a video game, they tend to incentivize behaviors that aren't always fun for a group of people trying to play together. The Elder Scrolls games mentioned would be a lot less fun as multiplayer games where your teammates have to sit around for half and hour waiting for you to get your skill use optimization rounds in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T06:40:56-08:00","id":1499745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499720#post1499720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backgrounds and rituals don't require XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're playing devil's advocate, but they should. WoD was, as far as I know, the first successful step away from RPGs as hard simulationism (as begun by Traveller and The Fantasy Trip), and so some of it's design is really weird.<br /> <br /> The Background/Merit split doesn't really make sense, mostly because things that should probably be Merits (Pure Breed, Spirit Heritage, Fetish, probably Rites) are instead Backgrounds because they were in the corebook. Although you can argue if Fetish should be neither, because it creates an oddity in how the game handles equipment. There really needed to be a rejigging of the entire system, but there is probably still a benefit for splitting Backgrounds into their own category. Notably having to spend points on things like Allies, Mentors, and Resources ties characters to the setting, which is much more interesting.<br /> <br /> There's also an argument for Backgrounds being transitory and therefore not requiring XP to buy, but in that case they probably shouldn't be buyable with BP either. Starting Background dots should be determined with something like Charisma+Finance or Intelligence+Expression.<br /> <br /> Of course, when the WoD was rebooted a decade and then again two and a half decades later both times the devs decided that backgrounds should cost XP (and by CofD2e Sanctity of Merits implied there was an underlying assumption of Sanctity of XP).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obtaining a shotgun would be a significant boost to your character's capabilities but few would ask XP for it. </div> </div> </div>I can see three rough viewpoints on this:<br /> 1) Equipment is transitory, and transitory things don't cost XP.<br /> 2) Equipment is a power boost, and power boosts cost XP.<br /> 3) Regular access to equipment is determined by other character traits that do cost XP, therefore equipment itself doesn't cost XP.<br /> <br /> cWoD mostly falls under the first category (although the existence of some backgrounds messes it up a bit), while CofD falls under the third category. WtA Gifts don't really fit either.<br /> <br /> Note that I, and most likely the developers, have made an unstated assumption: if you pick up a random shotgun you'll either lose it, leave it behind, or run out of ammunition in relatively short order. Many groups probably don't follow that assumption, but it's part of what makes abstracted wealth work.<br /> <br /> Then we get into stuff like Fetish. In WoD this is weird, because it creates this kind of item that costs character resources, but only if you want to start with one. It makes more sense in CofD, where Fetishes, Tokens, and other magic items are nearly universally Merits, and therefore cost XP (and in 2e refund XP if lost). Of course you get the potential for oddities like being gifted a powerful item but not having the XP for it, but it probably creates no more issues than WoD's 'but I spent 4BP on a Klaive, why does Geoff get one for free' stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm already houseruling most of that stuff. But I'm not sure where to go with Fetish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T07:59:18-08:00","id":1499751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499720#post1499720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backgrounds and rituals don't require XP? Obtaining a shotgun would be a significant boost to your character's capabilities but few would ask XP for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather be able to pay xp for rites. At the very least, to skip or speed up the learning time. Shotguns also technically don't require even Resources; getting spotted some cash and buying a gun doesn't even require an exchange of that Trait!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're called Gifts, right? Do you pay for the gifts other people give you? </div> </div> </div>Ah, but technically, the player is paying for a Gift for the character!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just playing devil's advocate here. Being someone who's actually done -gifts are earned with RP- i can definetly see why it's not the standard rules. But then again I think a carefully curated -The storyteller tracks what abilities you're using and gives them XP and automatic level-ups- system could be very good (With the player having more freedom to assign xp in downtime). One of the reasons I fell in love with <i>The Elder Scrolls</i> series was that with Morrowind and Oblivion you'd gain skills by using them and powers by buying/finding them, and you could loot everything that wasn't nailed down in Morrowind. It had some problems (Attribute distribution sucked shit) and Skyrim was nothing if not disappointing largely for abandoning what made things great (Perks are more important than skill levels in making you stronger for one)... but I digress. </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of advancement schemes for rpgs. They aren't even necessarily uniform for a given game; D&amp;D4e usually uses xp to step up character levels, but learning rituals involved shelling out money or finding them as treasure. Rarely, I suppose, you might learn them like Garou and Fera do rites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T08:18:35-08:00","id":1499755,"title":"","content":"<i>When we first started the campaign I was playing a hothead always getting into fights with criminals; the storyteller always had me mysteriously lose the bags full of money and guns I looted from combat. Now that I've spent XP for them I can't seem to get away from it. I've tried to mend my ways and go clean but I keep finding guns and drug money in unexpected places. So long as I'm not already equipped I Just need to search anywhere and I'll find something. I'm convinced a Malkavian is messing with me</i>. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A shotgun isn't a character Trait in the WoD games. </div> </div> </div>A simple mundane shotgun has more utility than most Garou gifts. An 8 base damage ranged attack is more impressive than most combat powers. Not to mention other uses like intimidation or grabbing attention. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the names are really bad descriptors of what they do. </div> </div> </div> You are given Gifts by spirits. I think the name is pretty apt. Maybe something like &quot;rewards&quot; would be more precise but by no means should Gifts be considered a &quot;really bad descriptor&quot; (and maybe thematically &quot;rewards&quot; would fit well with the good-doggy vibe that renown brings to werewolf) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . The Elder Scrolls games mentioned would be a lot less fun as multiplayer games where your teammates have to sit around for half and hour waiting for you to get your skill use optimization rounds in. </div> </div> </div> The storyteller is a moderator that should keep players from this kind of cheese. Plus like, pen'n paper games are a medium where a 30 second combat can last 4 hours but also any number of years can pass in a sentence. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Background/Merit split doesn't really make sense, mostly because things that should probably be Merits (Pure Breed, Spirit Heritage, Fetish, probably Rites) are instead Backgrounds because they were in the corebook </div> </div> </div>Agreed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Starting Background dots should be determined with something like Charisma+Finance or Intelligence+Expression. </div> </div> </div> This would give the impression that the WoD is more a meritocracy than the real world. Having rich parents does you more financial favours than actually being financially savvy. Plus playing a brilliant upstart has it's appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T09:50:59-08:00","id":1499761,"title":"","content":"If one wanted, one could simply get rid of XP altogether. Pathfinder has an option to have the DM declare level advancements as appropriate. RuneQuest has learning by spending time.<br /> <br /> Instead of asking &quot;Can I spend XP to raise this trait&quot; players, at the end or beginning of the game session could just ask &quot;Can I raise this trait?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T11:01:39-08:00","id":1499766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1499531-do-you-always-charge-xp-for-gifts?p=1499755#post1499755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>When we first started the campaign I was playing a hothead always getting into fights with criminals; the storyteller always had me mysteriously lose the bags full of money and guns I looted from combat. Now that I've spent XP for them I can't seem to get away from it. I've tried to mend my ways and go clean but I keep finding guns and drug money in unexpected places. So long as I'm not already equipped I Just need to search anywhere and I'll find something. I'm convinced a Malkavian is messing with me</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first bit isn't that unrealistic, you probably don't want to keep too much money or hold onto too many illegal firearms. A character like that also might easily have several large drains on their finances that far outstrip the wallets they pickup such as children or a Warhammer addiction.<br /> <br /> The second part is mostly strawmanning. There's probably few games which charge XP for equipment that won't let you refund or change the exact item, and your character going clean could very easily have involved setting up legitimate sources of income or removing the drains on your finances. Plus any reasonable ST would probably give you a refund on Resources if you stopped your frequent looting but didn't have any alternative income streams.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A simple mundane shotgun has more utility than most Garou gifts. An 8 base damage ranged attack is more impressive than most combat powers. Not to mention other uses like intimidation or grabbing attention. </div> </div> </div>It's also more likely to cause you issues just for carrying it, especially if it's not licenced. While my experience is coloured by being English, in a city-based game I'm not sure that many police officers would look kindly on you carrying that shotgun around. It's also bulky, and might potentially limit your ability to carry other equipment.<br /> <br /> Garou gifts are limited, but that's partially because Garou aren't that focused on the magic powers thing. Each one is a neat trick you can do, but they're not meant to relied on in the same way as Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Kinfolk probably get better magic than Garou do simply because they can access Hedge Magic and Sorcerer paths.<br /> <br /> Now I'd love to see more Gifts, if only because I'm always happy to pick up gender shifting powers no matter the game. But they're not generally worse than a shotgun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The storyteller is a moderator that should keep players from this kind of cheese. Plus like, pen'n paper games are a medium where a 30 second combat can last 4 hours but also any number of years can pass in a sentence. </div> </div> </div>Yes, let's put more work on the busiest player at the table! But honestly I've run games that do this, and it really just gets worse the more things you have to track. Each PC questing for a Gift is probably fine, having to track the relative value of every Gift every player has earned is even more annoying, and it only gets worse if you have to track multiple things.<br /> <br /> XP should stay the default for most advancement. I can see the potential argument for removing Gifts from that, but the default should definitely be either 'all Gifts cost XP' or 'no Gifts cost XP'. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This would give the impression that the WoD is more a meritocracy than the real world. Having rich parents does you more financial favours than actually being financially savvy. Plus playing a brilliant upstart has it's appeal. </div> </div> </div>I mean, it was a rough idea as an alternative to just saying 'everybody gets X background points and you can't buy any'. Social class probably should be factored in, but I don't think it should be that big a factor for PCs. Also it should probably involve multiple Attributes and/or Skills and dividing or capping, so that there's multiple ways to a good number of Background dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T05:57:07-08:00","id":1499854,"title":"","content":"In our party gifts cost xp like any other upgrade on the sheet but it's a little bit more flexible:<br /> If the pc want to get one that mean they have the xp to buy it. But when a spirit reward them by teaching them a gift and they don't have the xp to buy it? In that case i give them but i tell them that their character doesn't understand how to use it. <br /> If the pc want to unlock the gift he obtained previously he must buy it with the xp he earn then.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you can also describe the &quot;learning&quot; of the gift as something more complex. The spirit give a part of himself to the garou, but the garou must assimilate it correctly to develop the power, that is why it cost xp and also give an explanation on why a gift from an other breed/tribe/auspice is more expensive, because it doesn't correspond to the nature of the garou and is harder to understand and assimilate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T17:37:22-08:00","id":1500234,"title":"","content":"I always charge for the XP and you cannot use the gift until you've roleplayed out the communion and learning from the spirit. If you fail you get to try again and don't need to pay again until you finally learn it. It makes the gifts matter more and allows for interactions with the spirit world that take a break from the plot de jour. The only exception to this is when they are going on a quest to create a new Gift or find a lost one, if they succeed everyone in the pack gets it from the huge undertaking<br /> <br /> Since we mentioned backgrounds, I'm also quite willing to give them for free in game, as well as blow them up in game if the plot warrants. I do believe in letting them get them back and/or replacing investments in the chargen with something suitable if it turns out that it's impossible.<br /> <br /> The pacts and service to the Infernal forces in the WoD are different, they give raw power for a set of deals that get worse and worse for the user making them quite unplayable even at the entry level, and ultimatley taking over the character by the ST. If you're really keen on living through a fall like this and the mayhem it will cause, this isn't something that should be charged XP for, and is something that should be under the exclusive purview of the ST as it can wreck the game something fierce if everyone is not on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T13:25:00-08:00","id":1501830,"title":"","content":"Yes, I always do. I could maybe foresee a scenario where through some long journey a gift is learned though actions but at the end of the day thats what the XP earned is supposed to represent anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27749-welard","name":"Welard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}